From: NullCode1337 <contact.nullcode@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Do not request Qualcomm length-prefixed NAL bitstreams

MiuiCamera asks the Qualcomm HEVC encoder for length-prefixed NAL units
("feature-nal-length-bitstream" + "nal-length-in-bytes" = 4) whenever the
recording resolution is 4K or 8K. The encoder then also returns the codec
specific data (csd-0) in that length-prefixed form, which MediaMuxer cannot
consume: Utils.cpp's reassembleHVCC() requires csd-0 to start with an
Annex-B start code and otherwise returns 0, so the muxer track ends up
without hvcC.

MPEG4Writer silently accepts the track, but at stop() its
checkCodecSpecificData() fails, isTrackMalFormed() returns true and the
whole video stbl (stsd/stts/ctts/stss/stsz/stsc/co64) is dropped. What is
left behind is an audio-only MP4 with the video samples orphaned in mdat,
which is why 4K/8K recordings show up corrupted and are never inserted into
MediaStore, leaving the preview tab/gallery empty. 1080p does not set these
keys and muxes fine.

Skip the vendor keys so 4K/8K recordings take the same Annex-B path as
1080p.

---
 smali_classes3/fh/e.smali | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/smali_classes3/fh/e.smali b/smali_classes3/fh/e.smali
index d02e6ba..45340f4 100644
--- a/smali_classes3/fh/e.smali
+++ b/smali_classes3/fh/e.smali
@@ -774,7 +774,7 @@

     iget-object v3, v2, Lfh/a;->e:Lfh/r;

-    iget-boolean v7, v3, Lfh/r;->y:Z
+    const/4 v7, 0x0

     if-eqz v7, :cond_1c

